COSMO.rs reuses Clarabel.rs sparse CSC types and the QDLDL factorisation
backend as a numerical substrate. The ADMM / operator-splitting
algorithm, cone projection operators required by COSMO, rho adaptation,
infeasibility certificates, and termination criteria are implemented
independently and are not Clarabel's interior-point method.

Anderson acceleration in this crate is a Rust reimplementation of the
Type-II / QR / RestartedMemory accelerator from:

COSMOAccelerators.jl
Copyright 2021 Michael Garstka and contributors
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/oxfordcontrol/COSMOAccelerators.jl

The exponential-cone projection follows the bisection dual method used
by COSMO.jl, itself a modified version of the projection in SCS
(https://github.com/cvxgrp/scs). The power-cone projection follows
Hien, "Differential properties of Euclidean projections onto power cones"
(2015), as implemented in COSMO.jl.

The COSMO algorithm is described in:

  Garstka, Cannon, Goulart,
  "COSMO: A Conic Operator Splitting Method for Convex Conic Problems",
  Journal of Optimization Theory and Applications, 190:779–810, 2021.
  https://doi.org/10.1007/s10957-021-01896-x
